    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mitochondria generate energy in the form of ATP through cellular respiration, earning them the title 'powerhouse of the cell'.",
        "Lysosomes contain hydrolytic enzymes that break down cellular waste and worn-out organelles, often referred to as 'suicide bags'.",
        "Mature mammalian Red Blood Cells (RBCs) lack a nucleus to maximize space for oxygen-binding hemoglobin.",
        "Chlorophyll pigment absorbs solar energy for photosynthesis and contains a central Magnesium (Mg) ion.",
        "Human blood maintains a slightly alkaline pH range between 7.35 and 7.45."
      ],
      "id": "3rxffqz"
